   35|  98.9M|  // implementation:
   36|  98.9M|  //
   37|  98.9M|  // ```
   38|  98.9M|  // if i as u32 >= val {
   39|  98.9M|  //   *v -= *v >> rate;
   40|  98.9M|  // } else {
   41|  98.9M|  //   *v += (32768 - *v) >> rate;
   42|  98.9M|  // }
   43|  98.9M|  // ```
   44|  98.9M|  //
   45|  98.9M|  // We want to perform the same arithmetic operation in the two branches, therefore we can
   46|  98.9M|  // transform in something like:
   47|  98.9M|  //
   48|  98.9M|  // ```
   49|  98.9M|  // if i as u32 >= val {
   50|  98.9M|  //   *v -= *v >> rate;
   51|  98.9M|  // } else {
   52|  98.9M|  //   *v -= -((32768 - *v) >> rate);
   53|  98.9M|  // }
   54|  98.9M|  // ```
   55|  98.9M|  //
   56|  98.9M|  // It is possible to bring the "minus" for the second branch logically before the right shift
   57|  98.9M|  // using the following rule:
   58|  98.9M|  // -(x >> y) = (-1 - x) >> y + 1
   59|  98.9M|  // So we obtain
   60|  98.9M|  //
   61|  98.9M|  // ```
   62|  98.9M|  // if i as u32 >= val {
   63|  98.9M|  //   *v -= *v >> rate;
   64|  98.9M|  // } else {
   65|  98.9M|  //   *v -= (-1 - (32768 - *v)) >> rate + 1;
   66|  98.9M|  // }
   67|  98.9M|  // ```
   68|  98.9M|  //
