   70|  98.9M|  // in different ways on the two branches. `cmplt` returns `-1` if `lhs < rhs`, 0 otherwise.
   71|  98.9M|  // It is possible to use the `avg` SIMD operator, which performs `(lhs + rhs + 1) >> 1`. This is
   72|  98.9M|  // useful because `avg` treats numbers as unsigned, `-1 = 0xFFFF`, therefore `(0xFFFF + 0 + 1) >>
   73|  98.9M|  // 1 = 0x8000 = 32768`. Obviously `(0 + 0 + 1) >> 1 = 0`.
   74|  98.9M|  //
